{
	title: 'SYSTEM.md preprocessor: comments, if blocks, variables, includes',
	spec: 'SYSTEM.md is preprocessed before it joins the system prompt (src/host/system-prompt.ts; AGENTS.md files are not preprocessed and keep their comments). In order: HTML comments <!-- ... --> are removed (multi-line too); "::: if key=\\"glob\\"" ... ":::" blocks keep their lines only when the variable matches the glob (* any run, ? one char, other punctuation literal; directive lines stand alone with three or more colons; several key="glob" pairs on one line must all match; no else, nesting or escaping; an unclosed block or unknown key is an error naming the line, shown to the user, not silently dropped); includes: a line that is only @path is replaced by that file\'s text (preprocessed the same way, relative paths from the including file\'s directory, ~ expands) and fails loudly when missing, while @?path is replaced by the file if it exists and by nothing if it does not; include loops are an error; then ${variable} placeholders are replaced: harness (hal), model (provider/id), date, cwd (~ shortened), hal_dir, home (the home root), session_dir, hal_source (true when cwd is inside the Hal checkout). Unknown ${...} stay as they are. The result must stay byte-identical for the same inputs (caching), so no variable may change mid-session except through the inputs that already reach the prompt (cwd, model). Artifact old-system-prompt.ts (reference: its header comment and conditional-block code). Tests: comments gone; an if block kept and dropped by model; two conditions; unclosed block error; @ include, @? present and absent, missing @ fails, loop fails; variables replaced.',
	status: 'planned',
	needs: ['tm']
}
